hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16708","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Suhayb came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with dates and bread before him, and he said: Come near and eat; he said: So he took to eating from the dates, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have inflammation in your eye; he said: O Messenger of Allah, I am only eating from the other side; he said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled."
